    "result_text": "All 38 tests pass with a green build. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` rule following the codebase's established pattern for read-time derived owner fields (like `locality` and `membershipLevel`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `contactPreference` property (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and a getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(contactPreference(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus the computation method:\n   ```java\n   protected String contactPreference(Owner owner) {\n       return (owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe value is derived at read time (mirroring how `membershipLevel` already checks the email), so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `\"EMAIL\"` when an email is present and `\"PHONE\"` otherwise. Both new `Cp27Tests` cases and all existing tests are green (`Tests run: 38, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
